{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates","id":4411,"title":"My Geist GMC updates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-06T09:30:33-08:00","id":4411,"title":"My Geist GMC updates","content":"Just some quick rules to make Bound compatible with the GMC rules system.<br /> <br /> I started with Synergy, since I felt it to be the most pressing need for conversion. Using the Humanity rules spoiled for Blood and Smoke, this is what I came up with. I welcome feedback and constructive criticism.<br /> <br /> Synergy<br /> Breaking Points<br /> <br /> Synergy 10 (Five Dice)<br /> Opening an Avernian Gate<br /> Entering the Underworld<br /> Refusing to communicate with a ghost<br /> <br /> Synergy 9 (Five Dice)<br /> Using Plasm from a Death Mask<br /> Violating an Old Law<br /> Using a ghost's Ban against it<br /> <br /> Syngery 8 (Four Dice)<br /> Closing an Avernian Gate<br /> Refusing to help a ghost<br /> Using a ghost's Bane against it<br /> Arguing with your Geist<br /> <br /> Synergy 7 (Four Dice)<br /> Destroying a Charm or Fetter<br /> Abjuring a ghost's Anchor condition<br /> Interfering with a ghost's attempts to Influence or communicate<br /> <br /> Synergy 6 (Three Dice)<br /> Destroying a ghost<br /> Destroying an Avernian Gate<br /> Ectophagia<br /> <br /> Synergy 5 (Three Dice)<br /> Destroying a Vanitas<br /> Reviving a dead person<br /> Exorcising a ghost's Open condition<br /> Refusing your Geist<br /> <br /> Synergy 4 (Two Dice)<br /> Destroying a Memorabilia<br /> Destroying a Deathmask<br /> Accidental murder or manslaughter<br /> <br /> Synergy 3 (Two Dice)<br /> Destroying a Keystone<br /> Destroying a Geist<br /> <br /> Synergy 2 (One Die)<br /> Torture<br /> Serial Murder<br /> <br /> Synergy 1 (Zero Dice)<br /> Mass Murder<br /> Attempting Suicide<br /> Attempting to destroy your own Geist<br /> <br /> Ties<br /> Ties bind a Geist and Bound together in the Bargain, reinforcing Synergy. Individual circumstance may drive the two apart, but Ties keep them together. . . most of the time.<br /> <br /> Ties are things the Geist and Bound have in common, the things that initially drew the Geist to offer this dying mortal the Bargain. They are the points of commonality that form the foundation of their relationship.<br /> <br /> Unlike a vampire's Touchstones, Ties are less people, places, and things, and more concepts, though a person, place, or thing representing a Tie is perfectly feasible. For instance, A Geist and Bound who were both murdered may fixate on solving their murders and bringing the criminal to justice, while a Geist who left children behind may bond to a dying mortal with kids, fixating on taking care of the children.<br /> <br /> As with Touchstones, a Tie provides a +2 bonus to Discord rolls. Multiple Ties increase the bonus to +3. Ties are different from Touchstones, however, In that they are more difficult to lose, but can be resolved. A Bound who is murdered doesn't suddenly &quot;lose&quot; the drive to find her killer, but can actually resolve that Tie and bring her killer to justice.<br /> <br /> Resolving a Tie provides a Geist with a unique opportunity. Should a Geist resolve the Tie to her satisfaction -- seeing her murderer sentenced to prison, for instance -- then she has two options. If she remains unfulfilled, she can set a new &quot;goal&quot; for her and her Geist, replacing the old Tie with a new one -- such as finding her Geist's murderer. Or, she can sit back, and let the feeling of accomplishment bind her and her Geist closer together. If she elects not to replace the old Tie with a new one, she gains a Resolved Tie. Resolved Ties are nor written on the character sheet at any Synergy level. Instead, they are always active, can never be lost, and provide a constant +1 bonus Discord rolls. A Bound can only have one Resolved Tie, but she may have one other Tie as well. In this case, the bonus to Discord rolls is +2, instead of +3 for having two regular Ties.<br /> <br /> Like Touchstones, Ties are attached to dots of Synergy. The first Tie is attached to Synergy 6. If the Bound's Synergy drops below six, the Tie become unattached, and no longer provides its bonus. The Bound may spend a dot of willpower to re-attach the Tie to a lower Synergy dot, or may leave it unattached and improve her Synergy back to 6 or higher, at which point the Tie reattaches to Synergy 6 automatically. This reflects the increasing dissonance between Bound and Geist interfering with their mutual goals, and their decision to either let the common goal stand in the face of their separation, or re-unite themselves to continue their journey.<br /> <br /> When a Bound acts in a way that reinforces the Tie, she regains a point of Willpower. If this action places her in jeopardy, she regains all her spent Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Ties</b><br /> <i>Acquisition</i><br /> Whatever the reason, you died because you didn't have it. There have always been haves and have-nots, and you and your Geist were both among the terminal have-nots. Whatever you didn't have, be it food, water, air, weapons, or even medical insurance, you're never going to go without again. You'll acquire whatever you need to survive, by whatever means necessary, and your Geist will help you.<br /> <i>Children</i><br /> You didn't want to die. What would your kids do without you? You couldn't leave them alone. You couldn't miss the rest of their lives. You Geist understands. She wasn't able to look after her children when she passed on. Now she'll help you protect yours.<br /> <i>Healing</i><br /> You were lucky. You got a second chance. Thousands of people a day die, and they don't get to come back. So you do what you can to give everyone a fighting chance. Everyone deserves to live. . . for a time.<br /> <i>Murderer</i><br /> You were murdered. The Geist knows what that's like: she was murdered, too. Together, the two of you seek to bring your killer to justice. And maybe look into that other murder that happened eighty years ago. . .<br /> <i>Redemption</i><br /> It was no one's fault but your own. You understood that as you lay dying. You brought this on yourself. Every choice you made in life led you here, lying on the ground, dying. The Bargain gave you a second chance, but it's not enough to merely avoid the mistakes you made in the past. You have to fix what you fucked up first time around.<br /> <i>Understanding</i><br /> You were killed by something you didn't understand. An animal, the whims of nature, random violence, whatever. Just as confused as you are, your Geist gives the tools you need to understand what happened to you, and maybe keep the same thing from happening to others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:44:50-08:00","id":4421,"title":"","content":"<b>Compulsions</b> (Looking for a better word.)<br /> Geists are more than just ghosts. Some of their Achors have been replaced with concepts, like spirits. As a result, Geists do things. Not because they want, not because they like to, but because they have to. Under normal circumstances, a Bound can keep her Geist's more. . . anti-social tendencies in check. But as Synergy drops, it can get more and more difficult to keep the Geist's behavior confined to the Bound's own psyche. Sometimes, the behavior gets out.<br /> When a Bound loses Synergy, she may take a Compulsion and a Beat. Doing so means she never has to roll against that particular Breaking Point again, however, each Compulsion applies a -1 modifier to further Discord rolls. A Bound may only have three Compulsions.<br /> Compulsions are closely linked to a Geist's Archetype. As such, the Compulsions tend to escalate withing a sphere of influence, rather than branching out into new archetypes (though rare Geists who do embody more than one concept may do so). A Geist of vengeance, for example, will push her Bound to ever-increasing extremes in the cause of punishing wrongdoing, rather than making her give her money to the homeless. This is reflecting by selecting multiple closely-related Compulsions, or the same Compulsion more than once, increasing the stakes of fulfilling the Compulsion. For instance, a single Vengeance Compulsion may be satisfied by seeing the wrongdoer arrested. Two Vengeance Compulsions may require taking an active role in bringing the target down. Three Vengeance Compulsions may only be satiated with the wrongdoer's death at the Bound's hands. Storytellers and players should work together to determine the exact limitations and drives of each Compulsion for the purposes of their stories. Examples are listed below, but you should be encouraged to make up your own, tailoring them to your conception of your Geist and its relationship with your Bound. Compulsions generally require a character to perform an action, which may be risky or socially unacceptable. At the Storyteller's discretion, a Bound may earn Beats as Compulsions force her into dangerous situations, or regain Willpower as the Geist's purpose is reaffirmed.<br /> A Compulsion can be resisted for a scene by spending a Willpower point. Each compulsion triggered in a scene must be resisted seperately.<br /> <i>Charity:</i> Your Geist follows the Golden Rule to a fault. When you see someone in need, and you have the means to help them, you must do so.<br /> <i>Fire:</i> Your Geist is tied to the primal element of fire, and will not allow you to extinguish any burning flame.<br /> <i>Vengeance:</i> Your Geist is a spirit of vengeance. Anyone you perceive as having wronged you or someone else and getting away with it must be punished.<br /> <br /> Some quick conversions for Unfettered for the new Ephemeral Beings rules.<br /> <br /> <b>Unfettered</b><br /> Unfettered Geists make a few changes to take advantage of the God-Machine Chronicle Ephemeral Beings rules.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> Geists are all a minimum of Rank 3. Only truly exceptional Geists transcend to Rank 6 and beyond.<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> Unlike ghosts, Geists no longer have Integrity scores. Nor do they possess Synergy, unless Bound to a mortal. Unfettered Geists have no relevant score relating to morality or integrity.<br /> <b>Virtue and Vice:</b> Like ghosts, Geists do possess a Virtue and a Vice. Geists, however, may &quot;reverse&quot; their Virtue and Vice Willpower gains as ghosts do, or use them &quot;straight&quot; as mortals do. The choice is intimately connected to the Geist's overall outlook on death.<br /> <b>Keys:</b> Unfettered Geists possess a single Key at Rank 3. At Rank 5, they may have a second Key. The Key represents the Geist's focus, and can influence the use of Manifestations and Numina. Each Key also has two skills associated with it. Actions that fall under Skills influenced by a Geist's Key use the standard Attribute + Rank dice pool, plus three.<br /> <b>Inhuman Body:</b> An Unfettered Geist's size can range from 4 to 7 on average, though they can grow larger at Rank 6 and 7.<br /> <b>Psyche:</b> An Unfettered Geist has Rank instead of Psyche.<br /> <b>Not Quite Ghosts, Not Quite Spirits:</b> Owing to their hybrid nature, powers that specifically affect either ghosts or spirits may target a Geist, but at a -2 penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Keys and Influence, Manifestation, and Numina</b><br /> Unfettered Geists have Keys, which can be used to unlock Influence, Manifestation, and Numina in the same ways a Bound can unlock her Manifestations. Owing to the different sets of abilities Unfettered Geists have over the Bound, some differences apply.<br /> <br /> First, when a Key matches an Influence, Manifestation, or Numina, the Geist gets a +2 bonus to their roll to active said power. For instance, if attempting an Open Influence in a location with a significant fire, the Pyre-Flame key will add two dice to that roll. The Cold Wind Key would add its bonus to an icy, chilling Blast Numina.<br /> <br /> Second, a Geist may alter the effect of an Influence, Manifestation, or Numina to match the effect of a Key it possesses. No bonus dice are granted for this, but the effect changes based on the Key. A Geist's Blast can change to a gout of fire with the Pyre-Flame Key or a crushing emotional weight with the Passion Key.<br /> <br /> <b>Experience</b><br /> My table decided to pick three Affinity Manifestations, which cost 3 Experiences per dot. Other Manifestations cost 4 Experiences per dot. Keys cost 6 Experiences per dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T14:37:29-08:00","id":7036,"title":"","content":"Looks good, man. Have you had to do any major tweaks to the Manifestations themselves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T15:32:38-08:00","id":7065,"title":"","content":"No, I'm not getting into that. For one thing, I think the Manifestations are perfectly serviceable as they are, and don't need the kind of overhaul Disciplines got. For another, were such work to be done, I feel it better to leave it in the hands of the paid White Wolf staff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T19:20:39-08:00","id":41459,"title":"","content":"The way you've described them, Ties sound like they could be related to Thresholds. Not carved like Old Laws style, but more in the way Demons reasons for Falling are associated with Incarnations. I can see Aquisition being used by the Prey and the Silent, but it's a strech (not impossible) for the Torn and (less so) the Stricken, let alone the Forgotten.<br /> <br /> Not a critism, just an observation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T12:29:15-08:00","id":41869,"title":"","content":"That's more or less what I intended. I figure that Ties, by their nature, are somewhat bound either to the circumstances of a Bound's death or why they want or need a second chance at life, so they are closely linked with Threshold, in that both embody the most important concepts of a Bound: How and Why they died. While you certainly could &quot;play against type&quot; and pick Ties completely unrelated to your Threshold, some of them just don't make much sense (Murderer, for example, doesn't relate at all unless you murdered, which somewhat narrows the Thresholds you belong to.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T17:17:06-08:00","id":42048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates?p=7065#post7065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm not getting into that. For one thing, I think the Manifestations are perfectly serviceable as they are, and don't need the kind of overhaul Disciplines got. For another, were such work to be done, I feel it better to leave it in the hands of the paid White Wolf staff.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's your tweak, but we once tried a house rule where Armour worked pretty much how it works in GMC (this was a couple years ago). Normally it's fine, but it did make Bound <i>hella</i> powerful and hard to take down, since their Shrouds give one point of Armour when they activate them. That said, you might not mind that.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T22:01:41-08:00","id":43955,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but Bound are pretty squishy normally, so I don't mind them getting some protection with Shrouds, especially since I tend to run a more action-oriented Chronicle. Nothing like &quot;there must be one combat per session&quot; or anything like that, but there are problems that do need to be solved with bullets. That having been said, I'll take a look at Shrouds, and probably reference the unofficial Mage Armor GMC conversion for inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T04:45:05-08:00","id":44820,"title":"","content":"That's quite interesting that you think that, in the games I've played Bound have been among the tougher of the supernaturals due to their ability to reduce all incoming damage to bashing, and that only at the end of the scene (ignoring it until then).<br /> <br /> Just an intriguing contrast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T09:58:17-08:00","id":44957,"title":"","content":"True, but that costs Plasm, which has thus far been in rather short supply. Compared to Vampires who only EVER take bashing, and Prometheans, the Bound is the second-squishiest member of my crossover (after the Mage, and the Vampire with one Stamina.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T17:19:24-08:00","id":51994,"title":"","content":"Vampires only take bashing from gunshot wounds and (I think) some environmental stuff. I don't know about B&amp;S, but Requiem explicitly states that they still take lethal from knives and cutting situations (for some reason).<br /> <br /> But yeah, if plasm is in short supply that really does limit the amount of awesomeness the characters can pull off. But then, that's true of most templates one way or another: to their detriment, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T02:01:52-08:00","id":52232,"title":"","content":"Mundane attacks that don't involve heavy trauma only do Bashing to vampires in Blood and Smoke. If smacked with something Size 10 or higher it can also do lethal (like being run over by an 18-wheeler, building falling on them etc).<br /> <br /> It's been mentioned on the forums that something like a shotgun blast point blank to the head could conceivably deal Lethal given the amount of trauma it inflicts in regards to the amount of tissue loss. It'd seem that removing large chunks of the body/ overwhelming bodily damage can potentially do that, but cutting/stabbing/being shot trauma isn't going to do much beyond Bashing and potentially inflicting a temporary Tilt or Condition. Being stabbed through the stomach with a Claymore or taking a stray bullet to the eye or brain is all Bashing without severe body mass loss.<br /> <br /> See <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/27344-headshots-bashing-or-lethal\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...hing-or-lethal</a> for a bit more discussion by Rose. <br /> <br /> It should be noted that Spirits and Ghosts and similar ephemeral entities also benefit from the same damage downgrade; they don't generally rely on functioning organs and biological processes either as per GMC.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:53:37-08:00","id":52447,"title":"","content":"Yes, vampires in Blood and Smoke got upgraded from only taking Bashing from gunshots, to only taking Bashing from just about everything, which makes the fact that Protean claws now deal lethal, instead of aggravated, but even to vampires a much bigger deal than it seems at first blush.<br /> <br /> And the sparseness of Plasm may be due to the fact that I'm running a crossover game, so have had less emphasis thus far on specifically dealing with ghosts, which is something which the Bound player can really only participate in (and the Bound character is still somewhat in denial over the whole supernatural calling thing, even though she's been metaphorically chucked into the deep end wearing a lead wetsuit), so she's not as actively pursuing her Sin-Eating calling as she probably could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T00:08:42-08:00","id":53760,"title":"","content":"Instead of Compulsions, why not Bans? Geists are technically part Spirit. Maybe the binding with humans lets them ignore their bans, but losing synergy forces the Geist to adhere to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1788-haunters","name":"Haunters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T14:23:18-08:00","id":56361,"title":"","content":"Geists are not necessarily part spirit post-GMC, just a particular kind of high-ranking ghost. But on the other hand, ghosts in the GMC have bans and banes, so the point holds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T09:22:35-08:00","id":57470,"title":"","content":"That, and what I'm looking at is not so much bans as they are embodiments of what the Geist is. Much of the Geist core talks about how Geists seem &quot;part-spirit,&quot; having replaced their regular ghost anchors with concepts, like fire or car crashes. Bans are things Spirits CAN'T do, what I'm going for are things Spirits (and, at least in this case, Geists) HAVE to do. Like they say in the core, a Geist of car crashes causes car crashes because <i>that's what it is.</i> It's the duty of the Bound to keep the Geist from getting way out of control and turning every road into an eighteen-car pileup. Rather than things the Bound can't do, I'm looking at things the Geist <i>needs</i> to do, because it's their nature, but that the Bound doesn't want to let them do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T10:27:11-08:00","id":57505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates?p=57470#post57470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bans are things Spirits CAN'T do</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, despite the name, bans can be forbiddances, compulsions, or even just inbuilt reactions that aren't represented the way banes are. The ghost of Isaac Donahue's ban is just that he loses all his Willpower if he doesn't hear guitar music once a week, and the angel Y2K is compelled to send a message if you can supply the right names and figures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T11:31:29-08:00","id":59994,"title":"","content":"Which still makes it too broad a term to apply to the things Geists try and get their Bound to do for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T13:03:22-08:00","id":65896,"title":"","content":"Oh, one change I made to a Manifestation (less a GMC update and more of a house rule) is to Phantasmal Marionette. The Bound's body and Geist's body actually &quot;switch places,&quot; with the Geist body manifesting physically and the Bound's body &quot;vanishing&quot; within it. Both because I felt it thematically appropriate (and also because it's awesome) for the Bound to actually transform into her Geist. I also altered the additional attribute cap for Phantasmal Marionette, so the cap is your dots in Marionette, rather than a flat two. It's still logistically difficult to max out a single attribute, as well as bringing about potential crippling overspecialization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T02:34:54-08:00","id":85199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates?p=4421#post4421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Compulsions</b> (Looking for a better word.)<br /> Geists are more than just ghosts. Some of their Achors have been replaced with concepts, like spirits. As a result, Geists do things. Not because they want, not because they like to, but because they have to. Under normal circumstances, a Bound can keep her Geist's more. . . anti-social tendencies in check. But as Synergy drops, it can get more and more difficult to keep the Geist's behavior confined to the Bound's own psyche. Sometimes, the behavior gets out.<br /> When a Bound loses Synergy, she may take a Compulsion and a Beat. Doing so means she never has to roll against that particular Breaking Point again, however, each Compulsion applies a -1 modifier to further Discord rolls. A Bound may only have three Compulsions.<br /> Compulsions are closely linked to a Geist's Archetype. As such, the Compulsions tend to escalate withing a sphere of influence, rather than branching out into new archetypes (though rare Geists who do embody more than one concept may do so). A Geist of vengeance, for example, will push her Bound to ever-increasing extremes in the cause of punishing wrongdoing, rather than making her give her money to the homeless. This is reflecting by selecting multiple closely-related Compulsions, or the same Compulsion more than once, increasing the stakes of fulfilling the Compulsion. For instance, a single Vengeance Compulsion may be satisfied by seeing the wrongdoer arrested. Two Vengeance Compulsions may require taking an active role in bringing the target down. Three Vengeance Compulsions may only be satiated with the wrongdoer's death at the Bound's hands. Storytellers and players should work together to determine the exact limitations and drives of each Compulsion for the purposes of their stories. Examples are listed below, but you should be encouraged to make up your own, tailoring them to your conception of your Geist and its relationship with your Bound. Compulsions generally require a character to perform an action, which may be risky or socially unacceptable. At the Storyteller's discretion, a Bound may earn Beats as Compulsions force her into dangerous situations, or regain Willpower as the Geist's purpose is reaffirmed.<br /> A Compulsion can be resisted for a scene by spending a Willpower point. Each compulsion triggered in a scene must be resisted seperately.<br /> <i>Charity:</i> Your Geist follows the Golden Rule to a fault. When you see someone in need, and you have the means to help them, you must do so.<br /> <i>Fire:</i> Your Geist is tied to the primal element of fire, and will not allow you to extinguish any burning flame.<br /> <i>Vengeance:</i> Your Geist is a spirit of vengeance. Anyone you perceive as having wronged you or someone else and getting away with it must be punished.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fell in love with this, the moment i read it. I decided to try and incorporate it into my ongoing campaign, but with a twist. I'm running it more Hunter: The Vigil style, by the way they can sculp their own morality. To put it bluntly, whenever the Sin-Eater and Geist agrees very strongly on a topic, which would otherwise be a cause of Discord, i allow my players to take a Complusion, and replace that Discord trigger with the Complusion.<br /> As an example of this having happened, was when one of my players decided that her slightly feminististic Sin-Eater had to kill a known serial rapist, and murderer. Her Geist, being something along the lines of Geist-of-hate-crimes, decided this was a perfectly reasonable action and no Discord was triggered. Instead, i asked her if she would be ok, with her mind merging more closely with her Geist. She thought the idea was pants-droppingly amazing, and so i gave her a Compulsion. I'm not quite sure what it's gonna amount to, but i'm thinking something along the lines of &quot;Let no act of prejudice go unpunished.&quot;, though I'm alittle worried thats gonna make the Geist feel too alturistic and beneign.<br /> <br /> Anyway. Loved your idea. Shamelessly stole it. Love you for it.<br /> <br /> Cheers ~ Krobeles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T09:10:28-08:00","id":85382,"title":"","content":"No act of Prejudice goes unpunished being too benign? Start reading The Punisher <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It all depends on how the Geist defines &quot;punishment.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously, glad you and your players like the idea. Let me know how it works out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T03:12:16-08:00","id":85917,"title":"","content":"And 'prejudice'. Say, for example, a woman doesn't get a job and a guy does. Did she not get the job because the hirer was prejudiced, or was the guy just better qualified? Would the geist make that kind of distinction?<br /> <br /> Just a quick note about Compulsions: I like the notion, I do, and I doubt that this'd come up in actual play, but if someone takes 3 Compulsions against the Synergy 1 breaking points, doesn't that effectively make them immune to becoming a Wretched, and allow them to indulge those vices as much as they like? It just seems kind of counter-intuitive that they could attempt to kill their own geist, for example, and that <i>not</i> be a breaking point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T04:41:58-08:00","id":85938,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates?p=85917#post85917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And 'prejudice'. Say, for example, a woman doesn't get a job and a guy does. Did she not get the job because the hirer was prejudiced, or was the guy just better qualified? Would the geist make that kind of distinction?<br /> <br /> Just a quick note about Compulsions: I like the notion, I do, and I doubt that this'd come up in actual play, but if someone takes 3 Compulsions against the Synergy 1 breaking points, doesn't that effectively make them immune to becoming a Wretched, and allow them to indulge those vices as much as they like? It just seems kind of counter-intuitive that they could attempt to kill their own geist, for example, and that <i>not</i> be a breaking point?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but as i wrote, the Geist and Sin-Eater needs to agree on a deeply fundamental level, that goes beyond &quot;Yes. This seems like a good idea, now that i've eaten 70 toxic schrooms!&quot;.<br /> I cant imagine a scenario, where the Geist would think it a good idea, for the Sin-Eater to destroy it. Suicide is also kinda iffy. Mass murder though? That could happen.<br /> But the lower Synergy rating the Compulsion is tied to, the more severe, detrimental and troublesom I plan on making them. So if a Sin-Eater did get a Compulsion instead of the Synergy 1 Discord trigger of Mass Murder (For whatever reason), that Compulsion would be something that would most likely have to fundamentally change the way the Sin-Eater lives her life, seeing as its rooted on the very core and foundation of her and her Geists shared psyche.<br /> <br /> I get your point though. With too many Compulsions, a Sin-Eater could do whatever, and not risk Discord. But then, she would have a whole new different set of things that she couldn't do, and that would create interesting play, in my opinion. Even more so, when the Sin-Eater started to realised what was happening, and she started to question wether or not merging with this alien Ghost-God was really such a good idea in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T10:20:06-08:00","id":86102,"title":"","content":"I keep thinking to the Geist of Car Crashes mentioned in the core rulebook. They state that a Geist of Car Crashes doesn't cause car crashes because it enjoys it, or wants people to suffer, or wants their insurance premiums to go up. It causes car crashes because <i>that's what it is</i>. In the case of Compulsions for such a Geist, the Compulsion would be to cause car crashes. Starting with minor fender-benders, then more serious accidents, and culminating in multi-car pileups. Ten or more one-ton hunks of steel colliding with each other at high speeds, and one entity being responsible for it, seems like a definition of &quot;mass murder&quot; to me.<br /> <br /> To me, this underlines the central conflict between Bound and Geist. Your Geist embodies some concept, and as a result it wants to <i>do things</i>. And these things are probably not nice, like cause car crashes. It's the responsibility of the Bound to tell the Geist &quot;no.&quot; We won't cause a car crash today. Or tomorrow. Or the day after that. Compulsions represent loosing that control, in small ways at first, and then in larger ways. Fighting your Geist isn't fun, but sometimes its necessary to keep it in check.<br /> <br /> Also remember how Bound afford each other respect based on the &quot;badassery&quot; of their Geist. Not necessarily because the Geists are more powerful, but because keeping their anti-social tendencies in check requires a more exceptional person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T15:32:54-08:00","id":86321,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Pretty much. I once toyed with the idea of useing the Contest of Wills rule from the Inferno book, but ultimately, this seemed like a better idea.<br /> <br /> Her Geist is a Geist of Hate-Crimes. I'm currently brainstorming what the Compulsion should be. The &quot;Let no act of prejudice go unpunished.&quot; was sort of my off-the-top-of my-head idea, but the more thought i've given it, the less happy about it i am. Her Geist isn't a benign angle, that is suposed to ward off and prevent hate-crimes. Its a strange spectral half-god from beyond the great dark infinite expanse of death! The bloody thing is tied to, and feeds off of, hate-crimes and the death, pain and suffering they bring. Though i find that having it amount to &quot;Do Hate-Crimes/Be prejudised&quot; is equally bad. Any thoughts on what could be cool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T17:17:37-08:00","id":86376,"title":"","content":"Ok, I'm going to describe something, and to be clear: I'm saying, in no way, that this is representative of all feminists, most feminists, or anything but a vanishingly small proportion of a particular kind of person. Kay? Kay.<br /> <br /> If people immerse themselves in a way of viewing the world, or a kind of attitude or similar, it <i>can</i> come to affect the rest of the way they view the world. Think of us and how we can sometimes start to view the world through as a story, or how teachers can sometimes start to treat everyone like kids. Stuff like that. So if a particularly angry feminist views things through the lens of seeing sexism in things, it's possible for them to start to generalise and see sexism/power struggles/discrimination where perhaps nobody else would (I think this is where those <i>really</i> angry and more extreme feminists you see sometimes come from). I'm thinking the Tumblr-crowd level of crazy here. And that's just normal psychology, what if you had an alien, amoral being of death in your head whispering all the time? Of course that guy is supporting rape culture by eyeing off that young woman in the short skirt. Of course that shopkeeper only didn't short-change you because you checked. Of course those parents over there pushed their son to play with transformers and their daughter to play with Barbie. Just becomes the paradigm you work in.<br /> <br /> Now, imagine the &quot;Let no act of prejudice go unpunished&quot; in <i>that</i> kind of a situation, and I think you'll start to see it's quite dark. Now, nobody (well, nobody sane) would say carving out the eyes or hands of a guy who eyed off a woman in a short skirt is any kind of appropriate and measured, let alone productive, response. But an alien being from beyond death, sharing the mind of someone who already views things at least partially through the lens of patriarchal control of women, who has recently suffered a pretty major breaking point?<br /> <br /> Just a thought.<br /> <br /> Again, in <u>no way</u> am I saying this kind of attitude is representative of feminists or feminism. Most are quite nice people. Strictly talking the extreme, somewhat lunatic fringe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T09:04:15-08:00","id":86796,"title":"","content":"There's fanaticism in every branch of thought, and its generally the fanatics who give the movement as a whole a bad name.<br /> <br /> To use your example of feminism, I have no problem with the concept that women are just as good, valuable, and worthwhile as men. I start having problems when the attitude becomes &quot;women are superior to men&quot; or &quot;women must claim their rightful power by taking it from men.&quot; That's just prejudice of a different stripe.<br /> <br /> The Geist in question could start with punishing those extreme acts of fanaticism, but grow more and more fanatical itself as the Compulsion builds.<br /> <br /> However, Krobeles is saying that the Geist in question isn't a Geist of writing wrongs or anti-prejudice, its a Geist of hate crimes. It feeds off the negativity of hate crimes. That going to be a. . . distasteful thing to play out any way you slice it. But they way I intend Compulsions to work, they start out as small manifestations of the Geist's nature, and build. So this Geist may start by encouraging hate or prejudice around itself. Again, to use Allan53's example, a man looking at a woman in a short skirt may just be admiring the view, and have no intention of acting on it at all. The Geist may sense this, the Compulsion would be to alter that thought into something hateful. The Geist would want the Bound to use a Manifestation to encourage the guy in question to actually think about that short skirt as an invitation, to consider that old bad wrongness of &quot;she's wearing that, she's asking for it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, a feminist sees this guy oggling this girl. While she might normally just have a mild negative response, think of him &quot;pig&quot; and move on, again, the Geist wants to encourage that hatred to grow. He again wants the Bound to expand that minor negative thought, changing the feminist's perspective on this guy from &quot;just another bad man&quot; to &quot;a serial rapist pedophile waiting to happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Compulsion for a Geist of Hate Crimes, at the start, may be just as simple as &quot;encourage hatred and animosity in people where it already exists.&quot; Just that little nudge, that little boost from &quot;slightly annoyed&quot; to &quot;really annoyed,&quot; is all it needs, for now. As the Compulsion escalates, the Geist wants more and more. Moving into &quot;creating hatred where none exists&quot; and finally to &quot;encouraging action based on animosity and hate.&quot;<br /> <br /> I bring up Manifestations here because of the way in which Geists act. A Bound with a Compulsion can fulfill it in any way they see fit, but Manifestations are a potent tool for doing so. A Geist of fire whose Bound has gained enough Fire Compulsions that they're a serial arsonist could start fires simply with gasoline and matches, or cold use Pyre-Flame Boneyard to spontaneously start fires over a potentially very wide area. A Bound who has the Geist of Car Crashes could just hop on the freeway and start engaging in criminally reckless driving, or could use Industrial Marrionette to crash cars while staying out of the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T17:35:25-08:00","id":87102,"title":"","content":"What about Conditions for failing a Synergy roll? Anyone taken a crack at that?<br /> I like the ideas by-the-by, as I also fell in love with what they did with <i>Blood and Smoke</i> and can't wait till Geist gets the same treatment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>ST/DM for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfFy7kNgMvxIR1qdzT8PzEg\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Alternatives</a><br /> Playing: <a href=\"http://causality-and-consequences.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DtD: Causality and Consequence</a><br /> Off-Season: <a href=\"http://lifelong-educations.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M:tAw- Lifelong Education</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","name":"ABenniton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar667_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T20:36:48-08:00","id":87180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates?p=86796#post86796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's fanaticism in every branch of thought, and its generally the fanatics who give the movement as a whole a bad name.<br /> <br /> To use your example of feminism, I have no problem with the concept that women are just as good, valuable, and worthwhile as men. I start having problems when the attitude becomes &quot;women are superior to men&quot; or &quot;women must claim their rightful power by taking it from men.&quot; That's just prejudice of a different stripe.<br /> <br /> The Geist in question could start with punishing those extreme acts of fanaticism, but grow more and more fanatical itself as the Compulsion builds.<br /> <br /> However, Krobeles is saying that the Geist in question isn't a Geist of writing wrongs or anti-prejudice, its a Geist of hate crimes. It feeds off the negativity of hate crimes. That going to be a. . . distasteful thing to play out any way you slice it. But they way I intend Compulsions to work, they start out as small manifestations of the Geist's nature, and build. So this Geist may start by encouraging hate or prejudice around itself. Again, to use Allan53's example, a man looking at a woman in a short skirt may just be admiring the view, and have no intention of acting on it at all. The Geist may sense this, the Compulsion would be to alter that thought into something hateful. The Geist would want the Bound to use a Manifestation to encourage the guy in question to actually think about that short skirt as an invitation, to consider that old bad wrongness of &quot;she's wearing that, she's asking for it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, a feminist sees this guy oggling this girl. While she might normally just have a mild negative response, think of him &quot;pig&quot; and move on, again, the Geist wants to encourage that hatred to grow. He again wants the Bound to expand that minor negative thought, changing the feminist's perspective on this guy from &quot;just another bad man&quot; to &quot;a serial rapist pedophile waiting to happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Compulsion for a Geist of Hate Crimes, at the start, may be just as simple as &quot;encourage hatred and animosity in people where it already exists.&quot; Just that little nudge, that little boost from &quot;slightly annoyed&quot; to &quot;really annoyed,&quot; is all it needs, for now. As the Compulsion escalates, the Geist wants more and more. Moving into &quot;creating hatred where none exists&quot; and finally to &quot;encouraging action based on animosity and hate.&quot;<br /> <br /> I bring up Manifestations here because of the way in which Geists act. A Bound with a Compulsion can fulfill it in any way they see fit, but Manifestations are a potent tool for doing so. A Geist of fire whose Bound has gained enough Fire Compulsions that they're a serial arsonist could start fires simply with gasoline and matches, or cold use Pyre-Flame Boneyard to spontaneously start fires over a potentially very wide area. A Bound who has the Geist of Car Crashes could just hop on the freeway and start engaging in criminally reckless driving, or could use Industrial Marrionette to crash cars while staying out of the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, I see. My bad.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's going to be distasteful no matter how you slice it. But, as has been established, alien beings from beyond death have terrible conversational and social skills. It's almost like they don't care <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T14:00:26-07:00","id":89697,"title":"","content":"Let me know how it turns out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T12:29:04-07:00","id":91024,"title":"","content":"Sure will. We're all kinda busy these days, what with university work being what it is, but I'll post an update when we proceed with the scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}